<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Second Athenian League</h1><p class="st-meta">378 BCE – 338 BCE · capital Athens</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Alliance of Aegean states formed by Athens in 378 BCE to resist Sparta, with promises not to repeat the abuses of the 5th-century empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Spartan high-handedness after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-antalcidas">King's Peace</a> of 386 BCE, and a raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a> by the Spartan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sphodrias">Sphodrias</a>, pushed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> to found a new alliance in 378-377 BCE. The surviving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decree-of-aristoteles">decree of Aristoteles</a> invites <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> and barbarians to join 'so that the Spartans may allow the Greeks to be free', listing members such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chios">Chios</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Members kept their autonomy and constitutions, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> renounced garrisons, governors, tribute and Athenian settlement on allied land. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> sat in a council (synedrion) at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> that voted alongside the Athenian assembly and paid 'contributions' rather than tribute. At its height some seventy states joined. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chabrias">Chabrias</a>' naval victory off <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/naxos">Naxos</a> in 376 BCE restored Athenian sea power.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> gradually broke its promises, planting settlers on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/samos">Samos</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-357-355-bce">Social War</a> of 357-355 BCE <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chios">Chios</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rhodes">Rhodes</a>, Cos and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>, encouraged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mausolus">Mausolus</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hecatomnid-caria">Caria</a>, left the league. Reduced to a rump, it ended after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II</a>'s victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chaeronea-338-bce">Chaeronea</a> in 338 BCE and the creation of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-corinth">League of Corinth</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/second-athenian-league.jpg" alt="Second Athenian League" width="320" height="257"><figcaption>Image: Costas78 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_athenian_league_map.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>378 BCE – 338 BCE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Athens</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Chabrias, Timotheus, Callistratus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Second Athenian Confederacy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-358&amp;focus=second-athenian-league" aria-label="Second Athenian League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5271 812 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Second Athenian League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5591 1068L5709 970M5591 1068L5647 1055M5591 1068L5703 1128M5591 1068L5591 1068M5591 1068L5548 987"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5647 1055h0M5703 1128h0M5591 1068h0M5548 987h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" 